# libfontenc -- font encoding tables, and the layer between libXfont2 and the
# .enc files that map a font's glyph indices onto a character set.
#
# Packaged because libXfont2's configure takes it through
# PKG_CHECK_MODULES(XFONT, [xproto xtrans fontsproto >= 2.1.3 fontenc]) with no
# option to drop it -- so this is one of the X11 dependencies that is genuinely
# unconditional rather than an auto feature to pin.
#
# Not an LFS package, so it is pinned here rather than in versions.env.
SRC_URL=https://www.x.org/pub/individual/lib/libfontenc-1.1.8.tar.xz
SRC_SHA256=7b02c3d405236e0d86806b1de9d6868fe60c313628b38350b032914aa4fd14c6
SRC_DIR=libfontenc-1.1.8

# --with-fontrootdir IS PASSED EVEN THOUGH font-util WOULD SUPPLY IT, and the
# reason is that the mechanism supplying it is a silent one. configure resolves
# the font root in three steps (configure 19886-19896):
#
#   1. --with-fontrootdir, if given
#   2. otherwise `$PKG_CONFIG --variable=fontrootdir fontutil`
#   3. otherwise the literal ${datadir}/fonts/X11
#
# Step 2 failing is not an error -- it produces an empty string and falls
# through to step 3. So a build image without font-util, or with a fontutil.pc
# that lost its variable, installs the encodings somewhere plausible and says
# nothing. Passing the value makes step 1 the answer, and turns "did font-util
# get found?" from something this build depends on into something the font-util
# recipe asserts on its own account.
#
# A CONSEQUENCE WORTH STATING: passing it means font-util is NOT a build
# dependency of this package, and it is deliberately not declared as one. The
# only thing that would have made it one is the pkg-config query on step 2,
# and that query no longer happens. font-util is still packaged and still
# earlier in GRAPHICS_PKGS, because Xwayland reads the same variable out of the
# same file -- but this recipe declaring an edge it does not have would be a
# constraint check-build-order.sh enforces for a reason that is not true.
CONFIGURE_ARGS="--disable-static --with-fontrootdir=/usr/share/fonts/X11"
